(297157, 20334, 5573, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I will still submit the "digital art" types of entries. I really liked this one. I do understand that it blurs "digital art" and photography.<br/>However, The shot was taken during the challenge week and all rules were followed.<br/>I arranged the poppies on a glass candle holder, sprinkled with water and took a few shots with different exposures and metering.<br/>The PS7 steps I took are with the submission.<br/> <br/>Chris- here is the original image:<br/>//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=21428</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I will still submit the "digital art" types of entries. I really liked this one. I do understand that it blurs "digital art" and photography.However, The shot was taken during the challenge week and all rules were followed.I arranged the poppies on a glass candle holder, sprinkled with water and took a few shots with different exposures and metering.The PS7 steps I took are with the submission. Chris- here is the original image://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=21428', '2003-05-13 20:13:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(297332, 20334, 4494, '<td valign="top">Thanks Tarbini!  Great idea using that glass background and sort of flattening the poppies a little... it makes the final image really look great!</td>', 'Thanks Tarbini!  Great idea using that glass background and sort of flattening the poppies a little... it makes the final image really look great!', '2003-05-14 00:13:42.000000', NULL, 0),
